# ── Never commit these ───────────────────────────────────────
# Firebase Admin SDK service account keys. These ARE secret — they
# bypass security rules entirely and grant full project access.
# Downloaded from Project settings → Service accounts.
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
serviceAccountKey.json
service-account*.json
*.pem
*.p12

# Firebase CLI local state and logs (can leak project IDs and tokens)
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log
firebase-debug.*.log
.firebaserc
ui-debug.log
database-debug.log
firestore-debug.log

# Environment files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── config.js is a judgement call, not a secret ──────────────
# Firebase *web* config (apiKey, projectId, appId) is a public
# identifier, not a credential. Committing it is officially supported
# and is what you want if you're hosting one shared instance others
# sign into.
#
# Uncomment the line below only if you'd rather ship the code and have
# each person connect their own Firebase project via the setup screen.
